Do note that swap(...) is not a standard Java function; swapping typically requires three lines of additional
code. However, I communicated with the interviewer if I could use some psuedocode, and I was allowed to
do so. This is why constantly communicating with the interviewer is really important.
I was very much stuck while coding up this solution, but the interviewer always nudged me by providing
more test cases so that I could define the logic first and write it down later.
I justified the correctness and the 𝒪(𝑚𝑛) complexity of the solution and the interviewer moved onto the next
topic.
